  "names": {
    "order": "given family",
    "conventions": "One given name, very often after a grandparent, so the same few names run through every family. Everyday names are short forms of the official ones (Γιώργος for Γεώργιος, Κώστας for Κωνσταντίνος, Βάσω for Βασιλική), and people celebrate their name day as much as their birthday. Family names change with gender: a man is Παπαδόπουλος, his daughter Παπαδοπούλου; a man is Παπαδάκης, his sister Παπαδάκη. Endings show the region: -άκης is Cretan, -όπουλος Peloponnesian, -ίδης Pontic or northern. Surnames ending in -ου that come from a father's name (Γεωργίου, Ιωάννου) are the same for men and women, so `family` holds those, and `family_by_gender` holds the gendered pairs in matching order. Greek names are written here in Greek script. Albanians are Greece's largest immigrant community, and many also use a Greek name day to day.",
